{61}{Don't worry, Cappy!}{}{-4}{}{63}{}
{63}{Did I ever tell ye the story of how I came to own the Gypsy Shadow?}{Did I ever tell ye the story of how I came to own the Gypsy Shadow?}{}{}{}{}
{64}{No, you wouldn't tell me of it before...}{}{5}{ch 16, gf1027 0}{94}{}
{65}{No you wouldn't tell me of it before...}{}{5}{ch -15, gf1027 0}{72}{}
{66}{Yes, I remember.  The story of Jack Skellybones?}{}{5}{gf1027 1}{78}{}
{67}{Yes, vaguely.  Would you tell me one more time?}{}{5}{gf1027 1}{99}{}
{69}{Cappy no tell me story...[sniff]}{}{-4}{}{72}{}
{70}{E:}{}{1}{}{0}{}
{72}{Its just as well that I didn't tell it.  But I'll say that I ended up with the Gypsy Shadow on account of the most cold-blooded murdering pirate who ever sailed the seas of Arcanum, and his name was Stringy Pete...}{Its just as well that I didn't tell it.  But I'll say that I ended up with the Gypsy Shadow on account of the most cold-blooded murdering pirate who ever sailed the seas of Arcanum, and his name was Stringy Pete...}{}{}{}{}
{73}{What does he have to do with getting to Thanatos?}{}{5}{}{78}{}
{75}{O-oo-kay.  But how I get to Thana-a-at-t-os?}{}{-4}{}{78}{}
{76}{E:}{}{1}{}{0}{}
{78}{Well....there's a legend about old Stringy Pete, and I know it to be true.  You see, old Pete died more'n two hundred years ago, but legend has it he still sails the seas, a'hauntin' those souls who be unlucky enough to run across him...}{Well...there's a legend about old Stringy Pete, and I know it to be true.  You see, old Pete died more'n two hundred years ago, but legend has it he still sails the seas, a'hauntin' those souls who be unlucky enough to run across him...}{}{}{}{}
{79}{What are you saying, Captain?}{}{5}{}{82}{}
{80}{Uhh...I like pirates!    But I no unnerstand...?}{}{-4}{}{82}{}
{82}{I'm sayin' I seen his boat, and I know it to be real!  If you could get his boat, without gettin' yerself run-through by his ghost, you'd have yourself a boat...}{I'm sayin' I seen his boat, and I know it to be real!  If you could get his boat, without gettin' yerself run-through by his ghost, you'd have yourself a boat...}{}{}{}{}
{83}{Seems a little flimsy.  How do you find a ghost pirate's boat?}{}{5}{}{86}{}
{84}{How I find a ghost boat, Cappy?  Scary boat!}{}{-4}{}{86}{}
{86}{Years ago, I found a secret cove.  And there, on the beach, was with a unmarked grave...unmarked except for the sign a' the evil eye, which is the sign Stringy Pete used to carve on his victims.  I got out of there fast, without even looking for treasure...that could have been the place where he was buried, and if'n it was, its said most spirits return to their graves...}{Years ago, I found a secret cove.  And there, on the beach, was an unmarked grave...unmarked except for the sign a' the evil eye, which is the sign Stringy Pete used to carve on his victims.  I got out of there fast, without even looking for treasure...that could have been the place where he was buried, and if'n it was, its said most spirits return to their graves...}{}{}{}{}
{87}{At the very least, I might find some clues...}{}{5}{}{90}{}
{88}{Uhh...maybe find treasure too!  Play sword fight!}{}{-4}{}{90}{}
{90}{Yes, matey, I agree.  Here...I'll mark your map with the location of the cove. [Teach does so.]  Looks like you have a few options...buying, gambling or Stringy Pete...I don't like any of 'em, but good luck!}{Yes, lassie, I agree.  Here...I'll mark your map with the location of the cove. [Teach does so.]  Looks like you have a few options...buying, gambling or Stringy Pete...I don't like any of 'em, but good luck!}{}{}{}{lf9 1, mm 24, ru 2083, gf2479 1}
{91}{Thanks, Captain.  I'll keep you abreast of the situation.}{}{5}{}{0}{}
{92}{Okay, Cappy...I see you later...}{}{-4}{}{0}{}
{94}{Well, that was before all we've been through...would ye like to hear it now?}{Well, that was before all we've been through...would ye like to hear it now?}{}{}{}{}
{95}{Surely...}{}{5}{}{99}{}
{96}{Not really...but how does it relate to my getting to Thanatos?}{}{5}{}{72}{}
{97}{E:}{}{5}{}{0}{}
{99}{Of course I will.  Well, matey, by the time I could start growin' a beard, I'd sailed from one end of this land to the other, from the southern shores of Weeping Maidens to the northern ice-choked waters of the Jailer's Hump.  Ain't nothin' of the sea I hadn't seen, and most of it twice...}{Of course I will.  Well, missy, by the time I could start growin' a beard, I'd sailed from one end of this land to the other, from the southern shores of Weeping Maidens to the northern ice-choked waters of the Jailer's Hump.  Ain't nothin' of the sea I hadn't seen, and most of it twice...}{}{}{}{}
{100}{I see...please continue...}{}{5}{}{103}{}
{103}{At the time, I was runnin' ale outta Caladon, first-mate for a mean and crusty old cap'n who went by the name a' Jack Skellybones.  Half pirate and half devil, with the mouth of a blue-gilled she-demon and the breath to match.  Jack used to drink so much that we'd pray for tailwinds...if the journey'd take too long, he'd start drinkin' the profits...}{At the time, I was runnin' ale outta Caladon, for a mean and crusty old cap'n who went by the name a' Jack Skellybones.  Half pirate and half devil, with the mouth of a blue-gilled she-demon and the breath to match.  Jack used to drink so much that we'd pray for tailwinds...if the journey'd take too long, he'd start drinkin' the profits...}{}{}{}{}
{104}{Sounds like quite a character...}{}{5}{}{107}{}
{107}{That be the truth, matey.  Old Jack would fight ye if'n he thought ye breathed on him wrong...he had more scars on his face than most men had all over, and he could tell ye the story from each one, and never were they the same.  He was a hard man, but fair to his crew...and he loved the sea, matey, almost as much as he loved his boat, the Gypsy Shadow...}{That be the truth, lassie.  Old Jack would fight ye if'n he thought ye breathed on him wrong...he had more scars on his face than most men had all over, and he could tell ye the story from each one, and never were they the same.  He was a hard man, but fair to his crew...and he loved the sea, lassie, almost as much as he loved his boat, the Gypsy Shadow...}{}{}{}{}
{108}{Interesting.  What happened to him, Captain?}{}{5}{}{111}{}
{111}{Well, one night we was all drinkin' in the Sour Barnacle down Black Root way, and old Jack got real drunk, and started in with his stories...and as the night got on, they tales got taller and we laughed harder, and we were all havin' a grand old time...}{Well, one night we was all drinkin' in the Sour Barnacle down Black Root way, and old Jack got real drunk, and started in with his stories...and as the night got on, they tales got taller and we laughed harder, and we were all havin' a grand old time...}{}{}{}{}
{112}{And so...?}{}{5}{}{115}{}
{115}{Jack'd had one too many, and started sayin' as to how he was the greatest pirate on the seas of Arcanum, and how if'n there was anyone who thought they were crustier, then he'd a'have something to say about it...}{Well, Jack had one too many, and started sayin' as to how he was the greatest pirate on the seas of Arcanum, and how if'n there was anyone who thought they were crustier, then he'd a'have something to say about it...}{}{}{}{}
{116}{I see...what happened then?}{}{5}{}{119}{}
{119}{He started a'spittin' and a'holerin', and then, after upendin' every table in the place, he said that he was the greatest pirate who had EVER lived.  Tougher than Ruby Dirk, and Black Sam Bellamy...and even meaner than Stringy Pete himself...}{He started a'spittin' and a'holerin', and then, after upendin' every table in the place, he said that he was the greatest pirate who had EVER lived.  Tougher than Ruby Dirk, and Black Sam Bellamy...and even meaner than Stringy Pete himself...}{}{}{}{}
{120}{Stringy Pete?  Who's he?}{}{5}{}{123}{}
{123}{I don't talk much about him...I'll just say that Stringy Pete was the meanest, cold-blooded, murdering pirate who ever put to sail, and be done with it...there are stories and legends, and most of 'em are true.  He's been dead for more'n two hundred years, and people still whisper his name when they talk about him...}{I don't talk much about him...I'll just say that Stringy Pete was the meanest, cold-blooded, murdering pirate who ever put to sail, and be done with it...there are stories and legends, and most of 'em are true.  He's been dead for more'n two hundred years, and people still whisper his name when they talk about him...}{}{}{}{}
{124}{I see.  And what of Jack Skellybones?}{}{5}{}{127}{}
{127}{Well, after he said that, no one much felt like drinkin' after, and we put old Jack to bed.  You see, a pirate is mean, but he knows what to be jokin' about, and blusterin' about...and a'callin' out to the ghost of Stringy Pete ain't one of 'em...}{Well, after he said that, no one much felt like drinkin' after, and we put old Jack to bed.  You see, a pirate is mean, but he knows what to be jokin' about, and blusterin' about...and a'callin' out to the ghost of Stringy Pete ain't one of 'em...}{}{}{}{}
{128}{And so...?}{}{5}{}{131}{}
{131}{Well, a week or so later we were out to sea, and it was the new moon so it was dark, and a strange westerly had appeared, and brought in a bank of low clouds, thick as lamb stew...and then we saw the other ship, just a'restin' off the starboard.  Silent as death, and as still as if she was anchored...her sails tattered, her timbers rotted...and then we heard the screams...}{Well, a week or so later we were out to sea, and it was the new moon so it was dark, and a strange westerly had appeared, and brought in a bank of low clouds, thick as lamb stew...and then we saw the other ship, just a'restin' off the starboard.  Silent as death, and as still as if she was anchored...her sails tattered, her timbers rotted...and then we heard the screams...}{}{}{}{}
{132}{What happened?}{}{5}{}{135}{}
{135}{We found old Jack, in his cabin, with two daggers in him...one for each eye...and the sign' o the evil eye carved into his chest.  The very sign Old Stringy Pete used to leave on his victims.  We ran out to see who was on the other boat, but it was gone, a'takin' the clouds and the westerly with it.}{We found old Jack, in his cabin, with two daggers in him...one for each eye...and the sign' o the evil eye carved into his chest.  The very sign Old Stringy Pete used to leave on his victims.  We ran out to see who was on the other boat, but it was gone, a'takin' the clouds and the westerly with it.}{}{}{}{gf1027 1}
{136}{That's rather frightening...}{}{5}{}{139}{}
{139}{Bein' first mate, I took command, and ownership, of the Gypsy Shadow.  I've never laid eyes on that other boat since, and I hope I never do.}{Bein' first mate, I took command, and ownership, of the Gypsy Shadow.  I never seen that other boat, and I hope I never do.}{}{}{}{}
{140}{I see...what does this have to do with getting to Thanatos?}{}{5}{}{82}{}
{141}{I'm leaving...perhaps we'll speak of this later.}{}{5}{}{0}{}
{146}{I heard the news, matey, and ran over to her as soon as I could!  Ye won the Gypsy back!  Thank the stars!  And thank you, matey...thank you!}{I heard the news, lassie, and ran over to her as soon as I could!  Ye won the Gypsy back!  Thank the stars!  And thank you, lassie...thank you!}{}{}{}{lf8 1}
{147}{My pleasure, Captain.  Might we leave for Thanatos, now?}{}{5}{}{152}{}
{148}{Yay!  Cappy!  Go to Th-a-a-n-n-ato-o-s now?}{}{-4}{}{152}{}
{152}{Thanatos!  Surely!  Or wherever your heart desires, matey!  I'm a' going to give ye the Gypsy Shadow until yer finished with yer business!  She's your to do with as ye please.  Just try and bring her back in one piece!}{Thanatos!  Surely!  Or wherever your heart desires, lassie!  I'm a' going to give ye the Gypsy Shadow until yer finished with yer business!  She's your to do with as ye please.  Just try and bring her back in one piece!}{}{}{}{gf2719 1}
{153}{Thank you, Cap'n.  I'll do my best to take care of her...}{}{5}{}{156}{}
{154}{Thanks, Cappy!  I take care of her!}{}{-4}{}{156}{}
{156}{Thank you, matey!  And good luck...}{Thank you, lassie!  And good luck...}{}{}{}{}
